# What NOT to upload to Cloud Build.
#
# Without this file gcloud uploads the whole working tree -- 1.6 GB, almost all
# of it `data/frames` (28k JPEGs) and `.venv`. The build only needs the source,
# the seeds, and the small demo bundle assembled by `deploy/bundle.py`.
#
# Note gcloud uses this file INSTEAD of .gitignore once it exists, so anything
# that must reach the build has to be allowed here explicitly.

.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# 1.2 GB of evidence frames and 77 MB of generated clips. The handful the demo
# actually needs are copied into deploy/_bundle instead -- see the negation below.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. gcloud reads this file with gitignore
# semantics, where an unanchored `data/` matches a directory called `data` at
# ANY depth -- which silently took src/road_cleaner/adapters/geo/data with it.
# That directory holds the two gzipped files `locate()` reads, so the deployed
# image had no place lookup at all: dropping a pin raised FileNotFoundError out
# of /api/where and /api/cases/{id}/location, and the map just said "HTTP 500".
# Local was fine the whole time, because locally the files are simply there.
/data/
/design_artifacts/

# ...but the demo bundle must ship.
!deploy/_bundle/

# And so must the place lookup, belt and braces, in case the pattern above ever
# loses its anchor again. Named explicitly so it is obvious this is required.
!src/road_cleaner/adapters/geo/data/

.env

# Docs, by name. NOT a blanket `*.md`: the Gemini vision prompts live in
# src/road_cleaner/agents/prompts/*.md and are read at runtime, so excluding
# every markdown file builds an image that dies on startup with
# FileNotFoundError: analyst.md. Learned the hard way.
docs/
CLAUDE.md
